  "description": "T4030 Robinia - Pollard at approximately 8-10m retaining all lower canopy but reducing linear lower canopy on West aspect from 6m to 3m to previous pruning points. Justification: Stem cavities and habitat holes throughout lower stem at 4-6m indicating dysfunctional wood and posing a risk to structural integrity. Crown dominance to building restricting natural light to sheltered accommodation with elderly residents. Adjacent tree pollard requirements would leave tree asymmetric and under new wind exposure. Current height 17m reducing by 7-9m, current spread 9m, reducing by 3m.\r\nT0941 Group - Lateral reduce East dominance over adjacent garden from 5m to 3m due to moderate lean and basal cavity. No change to overall height or spread.",
